Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: declare the SSR filter's storage image format

Screen-space reflections were the last real feature gap under WebGPU. The filter
pass declared its output image with no format qualifier:

    layout(set = 0, binding = 1) uniform restrict writeonly image2D dest;

so glslang emitted OpTypeImage with format Unknown, and WGSL has no textureStore
overload for an unformatted storage texture. Tint rejected the module with

    textureStore: no matching call to
    'textureStore(texture_storage_2d<undefined, write>, vec2<i32>, vec4<f32>)'

and SSR was simply unavailable, with no error a game developer could act on.

rgba16f is not a guess. Its sibling shaders in the same effect chain --
screen_space_reflection.glsl and screen_space_reflection_resolve.glsl -- already
declare exactly that for this very texture, so the filter omitting it was an
inconsistency rather than a deliberate choice. The format is also provably the
one in use: the SSR buffers are allocated with get_base_data_format(), which is
either R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT when force_hdr is set, or
_render_buffers_get_preferred_color_format(), which RendererSceneRenderRD returns
as R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT. Forward Mobile overrides that to a packed 10-bit format,
but Mobile returns false from _render_buffers_can_be_storage() and therefore
never runs SSR at all. On every renderer that can reach this shader, the texture
is rgba16f.

If the SSR chain ever needs to run at another colour format, all four SSR shaders
must become format-parameterised together, the way copy_effects.cpp already does
it with OCTMAP_FORMAT.

Verified offline: screen_space_reflection_filter.glsl now translates to valid
WGSL. Not yet hardware-verified.

diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/screen_space_reflection_filter.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/screen_space_reflection_filter.glsl
index 6ca626ee5b..fefc198cf6 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/screen_space_reflection_filter.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/screen_space_reflection_filter.glsl
@@ -7,7 +7,16 @@
 layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1) in;
 
 layout(set = 0, binding = 0) uniform sampler2D source;
-layout(set = 0, binding = 1) uniform restrict writeonly image2D dest;
+// The format qualifier is required, not decorative. Without it glslang emits
+// OpTypeImage with format Unknown, and WGSL has no textureStore overload for an
+// unformatted storage texture -- Tint rejects the module with
+// "textureStore(texture_storage_2d<undefined, write>, ...)" and SSR is silently
+// unavailable under WebGPU. rgba16f matches what the sibling shaders in this same
+// effect chain (screen_space_reflection.glsl, screen_space_reflection_resolve.glsl)
+// already declare for this very texture. If the SSR chain ever needs to run at a
+// different colour format, all of them must become format-parameterised together,
+// the way copy_effects.cpp does it with OCTMAP_FORMAT.
+layout(rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 1) uniform restrict writeonly image2D dest;
 
 layout(push_constant, std430) uniform Params {
 	ivec2 screen_size;
